   "Atlas/Rudvalis/GaussianOrbitFrame.lean:3:0: The module doc-string for a file should be the first command after the imports.\nPlease, add a module doc-string before `/-- If a point-fixing group has precisely the remaining coordinate frame as an\norbit, then it lies in the already identified full code-frame stabilizer. -/\ntheorem gaussian_orbit_coordinate_complement (K : Subgroup gaussianLatticeGroup) (x y : MinimalCross)\n    (hx : x ∈ coordinateFrame) (hfix : ∀ g : K, g • x = x) (horbit : MulAction.orbit K y = coordinateFrame \\ { x }) :\n    K ≤ codeGaussianHom.range :=\n  by\n  have hstable (g : K) (c : MinimalCross) (hc : c ∈ coordinateFrame) : g • c ∈ coordinateFrame :=\n    by\n    by_cases he : c = x\n    · simpa [he, hfix g] using hx\n    · have ho : c ∈ MulAction.orbit K y := by rw [horbit]; exact ⟨hc, he⟩\n      have ht := MulAction.mapsTo_smul_orbit g y ho\n      rw [horbit] at ht\n      exact ht.1\n  intro g hg\n  let k : K := ⟨g, hg⟩\n  apply (gaussian_frame_stabilizer g).mp\n  intro c\n  constructor\n  · exact hstable k c\n  · intro hc\n    have h := hstable k⁻¹ (k • c) hc\n    simpa using h`.\n\nNote: This linter can be disabled with `set_option linter.style.header false`",
